From 2e5e378ec766ad942b71f77832b417035f0b89bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Romeo Mattar <romeomat.work@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:40:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] hw/sensor: add i2c-sim-sensor, a host-driven generic I2C
 register device

Emulating firmware that reads I2C sensors needs realistic, time-varying
sensor data, and writing a C model per chip does not scale. This device
is a 256-byte register file behind the common pointer-then-auto-increment
protocol whose contents are supplied by a host process over a chardev.
Each update carries a QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL timestamp and is applied by a
virtual-clock timer, so under -icount the guest sees the same values on
every run regardless of host speed; the device never blocks on the host.

A little generic structure covers common sensor and ADC chips without
chip-specific C: a register stride (16-bit register chips), one bank
selector (a register field choosing which bank a data range is read
from, e.g. ADS1115 MUX/PGA), read-set bit masks (ready flags) and
read-only ranges. Guest register writes are reported to the host.

Example:
  -chardev socket,id=s0,path=/tmp/s0.sock,server=on,wait=off
  -device i2c-sim-sensor,bus=i2c-bus.0,address=0x53,chardev=s0

Signed-off-by: Romeo Mattar <romeomat.work@gmail.com>
---
 hw/sensor/Kconfig          |   5 +
 hw/sensor/i2c_sim_sensor.c | 549 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 hw/sensor/meson.build      |   1 +
 3 files changed, 555 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 hw/sensor/i2c_sim_sensor.c

diff --git a/hw/sensor/Kconfig b/hw/sensor/Kconfig
index bc6331b..80fce28 100644
--- a/hw/sensor/Kconfig
+++ b/hw/sensor/Kconfig
@@ -43,3 +43,8 @@ config ISL_PMBUS_VR
 config MAX31785
